      "message": "[warning] Line 391: 🟡 The resize signal is propagated by mutating `streams[0]-\u003ecodecpar` from `read_packet`, but `codecpar` is stream-level metadata and not the packet-level mechanism FFmpeg uses for runtime parameter changes. This can make resize propagation ambiguous for consumers and fragile across API expectations. Prefer attaching `AV_PKT_DATA_PARAM_CHANGE` side data (width/height) to the packet when dimensions change, and keep `codecpar` as baseline stream metadata.",
